## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect per-tenant, private data path while supporting burst workloads, with per-tenant model versions, canary rollouts, and drift monitoring in AWS ML services.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint
- PrivateLink data residency
- Per-tenant Model Registry tags
- Canary rollouts and tenant routing
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK calls to register and route per-tenant models
const sm = new SageMaker({region: 'us-east-1'});
sm.registerModel({ModelName:'tenantA-v2', ...});
sm.createEndpoint({EndpointName:'multi-tenant-endpoint', ...});

// Lambda routing logic
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const modelName = `${tenant}-latest`;
  return await sm.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: 'multi-tenant-endpoint',
    TargetModel: modelName,
    Body: JSON.stringify(event.body)
  });
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-time streaming ML architecture, multi-tenant model isolation, and data governance within AWS's secure ML stack.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming inference patterns with Kinesis Data Streams
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint for tenant isolation
- SageMaker Feature Store for per-tenant feature management
- PrivateLink and VPC for data residency compliance
- Automated drift detection and retraining workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tenant routing to specific model in Multi-Model Endpoint
const invokeModel = async (tenantId, payload) => {
  const modelName = `model-${tenantId}`;
  const response = await sagemakerRuntime.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: endpointName,
    TargetModel: modelName,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  });
  return JSON.parse(response.Body);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses design for multi-tenant ML services with strict data residency, private networking, and production-grade reliability, including canarying, drift handling, and cost accounting.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Multi-tenant routing architectures (per-tenant vs shared endpoint)
- Canary deployments with automatic rollback on drift/latency
- SageMaker Model Monitor for drift and quality checks
- KMS encryption and data residency controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const endpoint = selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId);
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, payload);
}

function selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId) {
  // tenants mapped to endpoints or routing keys
  const map = {
    't1': 'endpoint-arn-1',
    't2': 'endpoint-arn-2'
  };
  return map[tenantId] || 'shared-endpoint-arn';
}
```

